    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38281" root="مخض" body-key="m">
    
      5 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تمخّض</span></b>  <i>It</i> (milk) <i>was,</i> or <i>became, agitated
in the</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِمْخَضَة</span>; (S, A, * TA;) as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">امتخض</span></b> .
(S, O, K.) [See also 4.] ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <i>It</i> (milk) <i>had its
butter taken.</i> (K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  (tropical:)  <i>It</i> (a child, or young
one,) <i>moved about in the belly of its mother;</i>
as also ↓ the latter verb. (S, TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  See also
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَخِضَتْ</span> and what follows it, to the end of the
paragraph.

